---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About Us — Nexus Wave Technologies" description="About Nexus Wave Technologies, its founder Kuldeep Kumar Yadav, accessibility mission, women safety priorities, spiritual learning and connected products.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-shell">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About Nexus Wave Technologies</p>
        <h1>Technology that serves people, not the other way around.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Nexus Wave Technologies is an independent technology service focused on accessible software, practical digital tools, spiritual learning and services that can make everyday life easier.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/apps">Explore products</a>
          <a class="button" href="/shlok">Explore Geeta Nexus</a>
          <a class="button" href="/contact">Connect with us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel">
        <img src="/assets/founder-desk.jpg" alt="Founder workspace at Nexus Wave Technologies" class="responsive-media" />
        <p class="muted">Independent product development from India with a strong focus on accessibility, privacy-aware design, responsible technology and community usefulness.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our mission</p>
        <h2>Build useful technology with a human purpose.</h2>
        <p class="muted">We bring software engineering, accessibility, AI utilities, media tools, spiritual learning and community support into one connected ecosystem. Our goal is to make everyday digital tasks simpler while also creating thoughtful ways for people to learn, contribute and seek support when they need it.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our principles</p>
        <h2>Accessibility, dignity, privacy and accountability.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Clear interfaces and screen-reader support are treated as core requirements. We also aim to handle personal information carefully, communicate limitations honestly, avoid exaggerated promises and design community systems around respectful participation.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our priorities</p><h2>Useful technology, accessibility and responsible product design.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Accessibility</h3><p class="muted">Clear structure, readable interfaces and support for assistive technologies are treated as product requirements.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Privacy</h3><p class="muted">We aim to minimize data collection, explain how information is used and avoid exposing sensitive details unnecessarily.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Responsible products</h3><p class="muted">Product capabilities, limitations and paid access should be communicated clearly rather than hidden behind technical language.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="founder">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder & product lead</p>
        <h2>Kuldeep Kumar Yadav</h2>
        <p class="muted">Nexus Wave Technologies is founded and led by <strong>Kuldeep Kumar Yadav</strong>. The work combines product development, software engineering, accessibility-focused design and community initiatives.</p>
        <p class="muted">The aim is not to build technology for technology’s sake. It is to create tools that are useful on an ordinary day and responsible when someone depends on them in a difficult moment.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility commitment</p>
        <h2>More people should be able to participate independently.</h2>
        <p class="muted">We prioritize semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, screen-reader labels, meaningful headings, clear focus states, readable content, reduced-motion support and straightforward controls across our website and products.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our ecosystem</p><h2>Products and initiatives working together.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Geeta Nexus</h3>
          <p class="muted">A standalone spiritual learning project centered on the Bhagavad Gita, with accessible reading, listening and daily shlok experiences.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list"><li>Bhagavad Gita reading and learning</li><li>Screen-reader-friendly navigation</li><li>Daily shlok and listening tools</li></ul>
          <a class="button" href="/shlok">Open Shlok Reader</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Nexus Plus</h3>
          <p class="muted">An all-in-one platform bringing together AI, audio, media, document, accessibility and everyday utility features.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list"><li>AI assistance and productivity</li><li>Audio, media and document utilities</li><li>Safety and support access pathways</li></ul>
          <a class="button" href="/apps#nexus-plus">Explore Nexus Plus</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Nexus Care</h3>
          <p class="muted">An upcoming wellness initiative for healthier routines, personal organization and specialized support resources.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list"><li>Habit and routine support</li><li>Private personal organization</li><li>Specialized wellness resources under development</li></ul>
          <span class="note">Currently in active development.</span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">The ecosystem at a glance</p><h2>Projects and initiatives.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Project / Initiative</th><th>Focus</th><th>Status</th><th>Highlights</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Geeta Nexus</th><td>Bhagavad Gita & spiritual learning</td><td>Live</td><td>Accessible reading, daily shlok and listening experiences</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Nexus Plus</th><td>Utility, AI, media & safety support</td><td>Live</td><td>Productivity tools, AI features, media utilities and support pathways</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Nexus Care</th><td>Wellness & routine support</td><td>In development</td><td>Habit support, personal organization and specialized resources</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Women’s Safety Campaign</th><td>Safety, awareness & active respect</td><td>Core initiative</td><td>Reporting, campaign participation, evidence review and community support</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Responsible support</p>
        <h2>Honest about the limits of an independent platform.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Nexus Wave Technologies is not a police authority, emergency response organization, hospital or law firm. A website or app report should never replace urgent professional assistance when someone is in immediate danger. Our systems are intended to create an additional support path, not a false promise of guaranteed intervention.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Connect with us</p>
        <h2>Build with us.</h2>
        <p class="muted">For product feedback, accessibility ideas, partnerships or community initiatives, reach out to the Nexus Wave Technologies team.</p>
        <p><strong>Founder:</strong> Kuldeep Kumar Yadav</p>
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:kuldeepky538@gmail.com">kuldeepky538@gmail.com</a></p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/contact">Contact</a><a class="button" href="/apps">View products</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>